  "id": "COMPOUND:33837 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "Calanphenanthrene A appears to interact with the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2 through a series of target relationships, suggesting a potential mechanism involving multiple pathways. The drug targets different kinases, including Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf and Serine/threonine-protein kinase pim-3, which in turn are targeted by Bullatine A and (+)-Parviflorol, respectively. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of the gamma-2 subunit, indicating a possible role in modulating its function. The evidence suggests that Calanphenanthrene A may influence the gamma-2 subunit through indirect pathways, possibly by activating or inhibiting upstream kinases that ultimately affect the receptor. The integration of these targets highlights a complex network of interactions, where Calanphenanthrene A could act as a modulator of the gamma-2 subunit through a series of downstream signaling events. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect supports the hypothesis that Calanphenanthrene A may exert its biological activity by influencing the gamma-2 subunit through a cascade of molecular interactions.",
